                                        "sense_id": "e8064c66-8a87-3f87-a8f3-163179e0ec87",
                                        "entry_id": "e54fdd66-c709-346d-a8ae-33e1089af0fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The 11th tropical storm of the 2005 Atlantic hurricane season, which caused catastrophic damage to Louisiana, Mississippi and parts of Alabama."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "faa55af5-c2af-4640-a633-4307c272939a",
                                                "sense_id": "e8064c66-8a87-3f87-a8f3-163179e0ec87",
                                                "text": "“It’s disaster capitalism,” the Aleph said. “All the profiteering that went down post-Katrina. It was in 2005. You’re probably too young to remember that hurricane.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b7c8a71-3f3d-363b-81b2-4158b8f42337",
                                        "entry_id": "e54fdd66-c709-346d-a8ae-33e1089af0fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A large-scale disaster, especially one with negative political consequences."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "metonymically"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
